> Basic Terminal Utilities

Essential utilities for viewing, filtering, and manipulating text and files.

### Viewing File Contents

`cat <filename>`: displays entire file contents to terminal.

`less <filename>`: interactive file viewer. scroll with arrow keys, exit with *q*.

`head -n <num> <filename>`: shows first <num> lines of a file. default is 10.

`tail -n <num> <filename>`: shows last <num> lines of a file. default is 10.
`tail -f <filename>`: follows file updates in real-time (useful for logs).

### Printing Text

`echo "text"`: prints text to terminal. often used with pipes or redirection.

### Counting Words and Lines

`wc <filename>`: counts lines, words, and characters.
output format: "5  10  50 filename" (5 lines, 10 words, 50 chars).
`wc -l <filename>`: counts only lines.

### Sorting and Unique Lines

`sort <filename>`: sorts lines alphabetically.
`sort -n <filename>`: sorts numerically.

`uniq <filename>`: removes consecutive duplicate lines from a sorted file.
common pattern: `sort list.txt | uniq`

### Watching Output

`watch -n <num> <command>`: runs command repeatedly, updating display every <num> seconds.
example: `watch -n 1 iostat`
